#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:1
msgid "ADR-0007: Random streams of stochastic elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P6.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:9
msgid ""
"Turbulent phase screens (P6.5) and detector noise (P6.9) need random "
"numbers inside transfer functions. Transfers are pure static functions of"
" their values and inputs (ADR-0002), so they cannot call "
"`ctx.rng(element)`. Results must still be reproducible from the seed of "
"the context (REQ-CTX-6), streams must be independent between elements, "
"and a cached output must be recomputed when the seed changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:14
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:16
msgid ""
"An element class sets `stochastic = True` to declare that its transfer "
"draws random numbers, like `time_dependent` and `observation_dependent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:18
msgid ""
"`Element.values()` then adds `random_key = (seed, *spawn_key)`, the key "
"of the context stream of the element (`(0,)` outside a context). It is a "
"tuple of integers: hashable (usable as a cache key, e.g. for phase-screen"
" spectra) and static for JAX pytrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:21
msgid ""
"`lumos.core.element.generator(values)` builds the NumPy generator of that"
" stream, `default_rng(SeedSequence(seed, spawn_key=...))`, identical to "
"`ctx.rng(element)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:23
msgid ""
"`Context.seed` is a property: setting it invalidates every stochastic "
"element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:24
msgid ""
"Draws that must differ over time (e.g. successive exposures) mix the "
"elapsed time of the clock into the key in the element itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:27
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:29
msgid ""
"**A `seed` setting per element**: simple, but duplicates the seed of the "
"context and breaks the \"one seed per context\" rule of REQ-CTX-6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:31
msgid ""
"**Passing a `Generator` object in the values**: a generator is stateful "
"(draws depend on call order) and is neither hashable nor a valid static "
"pytree leaf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:33
msgid ""
"**Drawing in the context and feeding noise as an input signal**: makes "
"graphs harder to read and moves element physics outside the element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:36
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:38
msgid ""
"Stochastic transfers stay pure: the same values (including the key) give "
"the same output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:39
msgid ""
"Elements outside a context always use the same stream; tests vary "
"realisations by creating contexts with different seeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0007-stochastic-elements.md:41
msgid "`random_key` is a reserved field name for stochastic elements."
msgstr ""
